    "top_frame": "The bullpen couldn't hold a four-run lead through five innings.",
    "what_this_means": "They got little from the lineup \u2014 11 strikeouts on eight hits, a .240 average that keeps shrinking \u2014 and when KC added runs late, there was no recovery. Civale pitched clean ball through five, which should have been enough in a home game. It wasn't. This team needed offensive traffic to become runs. Instead they made outs. The margin between staying in a division race and falling further behind is thin, and they just watched it get thinner. Shea Langeliers went 3-for-5, which is good work in isolation. It mattered zero against the final score. That's the shape of this inconsistency \u2014 flashes that don't compound into pressure on the opponent. You can't beat KC by hitting in spots. They needed the whole lineup to show up, or they needed the one player who did to carry them across the line. Neither happened.",
    "what_to_watch": "Now the question is whether Springs can arrest the pattern. Kansas City again, same division, same ballpark pressure \u2014 if the bats stay silent and the bullpen finds reasons to sweat, this becomes a two-game slide that feels like a statement about who wins in this division. Tonight will show if yesterday was a stall or the start of something worse.",
